# Family and home (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, phase 7, the family theme): chains. One of a family says what's on their
# mind (talk.family), the other answers as they are, and sometimes the first has the last word. The answers are
# concepts of their own, so each is the answerer's best rule:
#
#   family.worry_answer   answering a worry; conv.f7_worry says which (money, shop, watch, worn, roofless, damp,
#                         noise, child, child_fret, hurt_you, hurt_me, grief, kin, move, death)
#   family.tease_answer   answering a tease or grumble; conv.f7_tease (chore, duty, spend, kin, envy, pups, dare,
#                         ale, snap, flirt, jibe)
#   family.share_answer   answering news, a memory, a plan, a fond word; conv.f7_share, or conv.f7_asked when a
#                         friend asked after their family
#   family.answer_parent  a son or daughter answering their mother or father; conv.f7_pc
#   family.answer_child   a mother or father answering their son or daughter; conv.f7_cp
#   family.settle         the opener's last word, on the tone of the answer: conv.f7_chain (worry, tease, share,
#                         pc, cp) and conv.f7_tone (kind, sharp, jest, fret, eager), set by the answer
#
# A chain's later beats take only the best tier, so every reply keyed to what was said has priority 1: it always
# outranks the replies by temper or humour alone, which are kept for openers that set no key. An answer with no tone
# of its own ends the talk; one that hands on to family.settle remembers its tone.
#
# Careful with names: between spouses, the one spoken to is #dear# or #pet#; #self.child# is the speaker's child, and
# lines about a small one need the parent young enough (self.age<=36) for the child to be a pup. Everyday remarks keep
# a cooldown of a day or two, serious ones half a day. (A rule's `say` can't take ^m/^f: those work in grammar only, so
# a line for one sex is a rule of its own, with other.sex or self.sex.)

# =============================================================================================== Spouses: worries

rule f7_sp_rent
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_worry=money f7_chain=worry} Rent's due on Restday and the jar's light, #dear#. | {f7_worry=money f7_chain=worry} I counted the jar twice. It came out the same both times. | {f7_worry=money f7_chain=worry} We're short for the rent again. Not by much. By enough. | {f7_worry=money f7_chain=worry} The landlord stopped me on the stair. Smiling. I don't like it when he smiles.
then other: family.worry_answer

rule f7_sp_rent_home
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.wealth=poor|destitute here.place=home here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_worry=money f7_chain=worry} Don't light the second candle. We'll manage with one. | {f7_worry=money f7_chain=worry} I watered the soup. Don't tell me you can taste it. | {f7_worry=money f7_chain=worry} The landlord's boy was at the door. I said you were out. | {f7_worry=money f7_chain=worry} I've had the jar out again. It doesn't fill by looking at it.
then other: family.worry_answer

rule f7_sp_owes
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.owes=yes
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_worry=money f7_chain=worry} I saw the one we owe in the street. I crossed over. | {f7_worry=money f7_chain=worry} How long can we keep putting them off, #dear#? | {f7_worry=money f7_chain=worry} I had a letter about the debt. I've not opened it. It's under the bread crock. | {f7_worry=money f7_chain=worry} They want it by the new month. All of it.
then other: family.worry_answer

rule f7_sp_dole
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.on_dole=yes
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_worry=money f7_chain=worry} I queued for the parish bread. Don't say anything. | {f7_worry=money f7_chain=worry} Two hours in the line for one loaf. One. | {f7_worry=money f7_chain=worry} The priest looked at me kindly. I nearly threw the loaf at him. | {f7_worry=money f7_chain=worry} Our old neighbour was in the dole line. We both pretended not to see.
then other: family.worry_answer

rule f7_sp_hungry
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.hungry=yes self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say {f7_worry=money f7_chain=worry} There's nothing in the pot but water and hope. | {f7_worry=money f7_chain=worry} You have the heel of the loaf. I'm not hungry. I'm not. | {f7_worry=money f7_chain=worry} I could eat the table. We may have to. | {f7_worry=money f7_chain=worry} I dreamt of a ham. A whole ham. I woke up chewing the blanket.
then other: family.worry_answer

rule f7_sp_failing
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.business=failing
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
priority 1
say {f7_worry=shop f7_chain=worry} Not one customer today. Not one. | {f7_worry=shop f7_chain=worry} I did the sums. Then I did them again, hoping. | {f7_worry=shop f7_chain=worry} If the shop goes, what do we do? Truly? | {f7_worry=shop f7_chain=worry} I've stock going stale on the shelf and nobody through the door.
then other: family.worry_answer

rule f7_sp_guard
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.role=guard
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_worry=watch f7_chain=worry} Night watch again this week. | {f7_worry=watch f7_chain=worry} There was a knife out by the gate today. I'm fine. I'm fine. | {f7_worry=watch f7_chain=worry} The captain wants more of us on the walls. | {f7_worry=watch f7_chain=worry} A drunk took a swing at me. Missed. Mostly.
then other: family.worry_answer

rule f7_sp_worn
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.tired=yes self.working=yes
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_worry=worn f7_chain=worry} I can't keep these hours, #dear#. Something has to give. | {f7_worry=worn f7_chain=worry} I fell asleep standing up today. Standing! | {f7_worry=worn f7_chain=worry} My paws are worn to the pads. | {f7_worry=worn f7_chain=worry} Dawn to dark, and they want me in early tomorrow.
then other: family.worry_answer

rule f7_sp_homeless
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.homeless=yes
does tell.self
cooldown 12h
priority 1
say {f7_worry=roofless f7_chain=worry} Another night in a doorway, #dear#. Lie close. | {f7_worry=roofless f7_chain=worry} I found a barn with half a roof. It's something. | {f7_worry=roofless f7_chain=worry} Don't look at me like that. We'll have a door again. | {f7_worry=roofless f7_chain=worry} They moved us on from the chapel porch. Kindly, but they moved us on.
then other: family.worry_answer

rule f7_sp_sump_damp
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.quarter=sump
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_worry=damp f7_chain=worry} The damp's in the bedding again. | {f7_worry=damp f7_chain=worry} Water came under the door in the night. My boots are swimming. | {f7_worry=damp f7_chain=worry} The rats have found the meal sack. Again. | {f7_worry=damp f7_chain=worry} There's green on the wall behind the bed. Green, #dear#.
then other: family.worry_answer

rule f7_sp_nervy_night
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.temper=nervy here.time=night
does tell.self
cooldown 1d
say {f7_worry=noise f7_chain=worry} Did you bar the door? Are you sure? | {f7_worry=noise f7_chain=worry} What was that? Listen. | {f7_worry=noise f7_chain=worry} I heard someone on the stair. I did. | {f7_worry=noise f7_chain=worry} Something's scratching at the shutter. Don't laugh.
then other: family.worry_answer

rule f7_sp_child_worry
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.child self.age<=40
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_worry=child f7_chain=worry} #self.child# hardly ate a thing at #supper#. | {f7_worry=child f7_chain=worry} Did #self.child# seem quiet to you? Too quiet? | {f7_worry=child f7_chain=worry} #self.child# came home with a split lip and won't say who. | {f7_worry=child f7_chain=worry} #self.child# lied to me today. Looked me in the eye and lied.
then other: family.worry_answer

rule f7_sp_child_worry_nervy
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.child self.temper=nervy self.age<=40
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_worry=child_fret f7_chain=worry} #self.child# is late. #self.child# is never late. | {f7_worry=child_fret f7_chain=worry} Is #self.child# warm enough, do you think? That blanket's thin. | {f7_worry=child_fret f7_chain=worry} I keep dreaming #self.child# falls in the river. | {f7_worry=child_fret f7_chain=worry} #self.child# was coughing in the night. Did you hear?
then other: family.worry_answer

rule f7_sp_child_grown
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.child self.age>=48
does tell.self
cooldown 3d
say {f7_worry=child f7_chain=worry} #self.child# hasn't been round in a fortnight. | {f7_worry=child f7_chain=worry} Do you think #self.child# is happy? Truly? | {f7_worry=child f7_chain=worry} I saw #self.child# at the market. Thin, I thought. | {f7_worry=child f7_chain=worry} #self.child# never asks us for anything. I wish #self.child_they# would.
then other: family.worry_answer

rule f7_sp_hurt
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses other.injured=light|bad
does tell.self
cooldown 6h
priority 1
say {f7_worry=hurt_you f7_chain=worry} Sit down. Let me see it. | {f7_worry=hurt_you f7_chain=worry} You're limping. Don't tell me you're not. | {f7_worry=hurt_you f7_chain=worry} Who did this to you? | {f7_worry=hurt_you f7_chain=worry} Hold still. I'll bind it.
then other: family.worry_answer

rule f7_sp_hurt_self
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.injured=bad
does tell.self
cooldown 6h
priority 2
say {f7_worry=hurt_me f7_chain=worry} Help me to the chair, #dear#. Slowly. | {f7_worry=hurt_me f7_chain=worry} I'll be no use at work for days. | {f7_worry=hurt_me f7_chain=worry} Don't fuss. Well. Fuss a bit. | {f7_worry=hurt_me f7_chain=worry} I can't get my boot off. Will you?
then other: family.worry_answer

rule f7_sp_grief
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.mourning=kin
does tell.self
cooldown 6h
priority 3
say {f7_worry=grief f7_chain=worry} I keep waiting for the door to open. | {f7_worry=grief f7_chain=worry} I can't do the funeral things. I can't. | {f7_worry=grief f7_chain=worry} Hold me a while. Don't say anything. | {f7_worry=grief f7_chain=worry} I found their old scarf in the chest. It still smells of them.
then other: family.worry_answer

rule f7_sp_grief_friend
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.mourning=friend
does tell.self
cooldown 12h
priority 1
say {f7_worry=grief f7_chain=worry} I keep thinking of the last thing I said to them. It was about the weather. | {f7_worry=grief f7_chain=worry} We were meant to drink together at the festival. | {f7_worry=grief f7_chain=worry} Funny. I'd not seen them in a month, and now I miss them every hour. | {f7_worry=grief f7_chain=worry} I owed them a jar. I'll never pay it now.
then other: family.worry_answer

rule f7_sp_mother_ill
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.mother
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_worry=kin f7_chain=worry} I should look in on #mum#. She sounded chesty. | {f7_worry=kin f7_chain=worry} #mum.capitalize# says she's fine. She always says she's fine. | {f7_worry=kin f7_chain=worry} I'm worried about #mum# on those stairs. | {f7_worry=kin f7_chain=worry} #mum.capitalize# gave away her good shawl. She's never given away anything.
then other: family.worry_answer

rule f7_sp_father_old
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.father
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_worry=kin f7_chain=worry} #dad.capitalize# forgot my name yesterday. Just for a breath. | {f7_worry=kin f7_chain=worry} #dad.capitalize# won't stop working. He'll drop where he stands. | {f7_worry=kin f7_chain=worry} Should #dad# come and live with us? | {f7_worry=kin f7_chain=worry} #dad.capitalize# was out in the yard at midnight, looking for a goat he had as a pup.
then other: family.worry_answer

rule f7_sp_restless
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.drive=restless
does tell.self
cooldown 3d
say {f7_worry=move f7_chain=worry} What if we went? Somewhere new. Just packed and went. | {f7_worry=move f7_chain=worry} I can't spend my whole life on this street, #dear#. | {f7_worry=move f7_chain=worry} They say there's work in the other towns. Land, even. | {f7_worry=move f7_chain=worry} A carter said there's houses going cheap down south. Houses, #dear#.
then other: family.worry_answer

rule f7_sp_old_death
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.stage=old other.stage=old world.death=recent
does tell.self
cooldown 3d
say {f7_worry=death f7_chain=worry} Another one gone. Promise me you'll go second. | {f7_worry=death f7_chain=worry} When it's my turn, don't let them sing that dreary hymn. | {f7_worry=death f7_chain=worry} Which of us will it be first, do you think? | {f7_worry=death f7_chain=worry} We're running out of friends to bury. Then it's us.
then other: family.worry_answer

# =============================================================================================== Spouses: teasing and bickering

rule f7_sp_inlaw_mother
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses other.mother
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_tease=kin f7_chain=tease} #other.mother# came by. She moved all the pots. | {f7_tease=kin f7_chain=tease} Your mother asked when we're giving her more grandpups. In the street. | {f7_tease=kin f7_chain=tease} #other.mother# says I put too much salt in. To my face. | {f7_tease=kin f7_chain=tease} #other.mother# brought us a cushion. She says ours are a disgrace.
then other: family.tease_answer

rule f7_sp_inlaw_father
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses other.father
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_tease=kin f7_chain=tease} #other.father# told me how to hold a broom. A broom. | {f7_tease=kin f7_chain=tease} Your father's been telling everyone at the well about his knee. Everyone. | {f7_tease=kin f7_chain=tease} #other.father# shook my paw today. Like he meant it, for once. | {f7_tease=kin f7_chain=tease} #other.father# called me by your old sweetheart's name. Twice.
then other: family.tease_answer

rule f7_sp_short_door
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.temper=short here.place=home
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_tease=chore f7_chain=tease} Who left the door wide open? Were you raised in a field? | {f7_tease=chore f7_chain=tease} Mud. On the floor. Paw-shaped mud. | {f7_tease=chore f7_chain=tease} Is it so hard to put the knife back where it lives? | {f7_tease=chore f7_chain=tease} You've hung your wet cloak on my chair. My chair.
then other: family.tease_answer

rule f7_sp_chores
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses here.place=home
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_tease=chore f7_chain=tease} It was your turn on the water. Yesterday too. | {f7_tease=chore f7_chain=tease} The shutter's still hanging off. Since spring. | {f7_tease=chore f7_chain=tease} I scrubbed the step. Did you notice? You didn't notice. | {f7_tease=chore f7_chain=tease} You said you'd mend the chair. The chair remembers.
then other: family.tease_answer

rule f7_sp_winter_feet
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses here.season=winter here.place=home
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_tease=chore f7_chain=tease} Put your cold feet anywhere but on me. | {f7_tease=chore f7_chain=tease} You've had the blanket all night. All of it. | {f7_tease=chore f7_chain=tease} The fire's out and it was your turn to bank it. | {f7_tease=chore f7_chain=tease} You let the cold in every time you go out to the yard. Every time.
then other: family.tease_answer

rule f7_sp_summer_fur
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses here.season=summer here.place=home
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_tease=chore f7_chain=tease} You're shedding on everything. The bread had fur in it. | {f7_tease=chore f7_chain=tease} Don't lie so close, it's like sleeping by an oven. | {f7_tease=chore f7_chain=tease} Brush yourself outside, I'm begging you. | {f7_tease=chore f7_chain=tease} There's more of your coat on the bed than on you.
then other: family.tease_answer

rule f7_sp_dawn_snore
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses here.time=dawn here.place=home
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_tease=chore f7_chain=tease} You were snoring again. Like a saw through wet wood. | {f7_tease=chore f7_chain=tease} You talked in your sleep. Who's Hettie? | {f7_tease=chore f7_chain=tease} You kicked me twice. I counted. | {f7_tease=chore f7_chain=tease} You were chasing something in your sleep. Your legs were going like a pup's.
then other: family.tease_answer

rule f7_sp_rich_spend
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.wealth=rich
does ask.detail
cooldown 2d
say {f7_tease=spend f7_chain=tease} You've ordered new hangings for the front room? Again? | {f7_tease=spend f7_chain=tease} You spent how much on that brooch? | {f7_tease=spend f7_chain=tease} The silversmith sent his bill. I want to know what we bought. | {f7_tease=spend f7_chain=tease} Another horse. We've four. You ride one.
then other: family.tease_answer

rule f7_sp_heights_dinner
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.quarter=heights
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_tease=duty f7_chain=tease} We're asked to dine with the Ashcombes again. Do try to be pleasant. | {f7_tease=duty f7_chain=tease} Lady Ashcombe will be there. Don't mention her nephew. Or her teeth. | {f7_tease=duty f7_chain=tease} And this time, no talk of drains at the table. | {f7_tease=duty f7_chain=tease} The Vanes are giving a musical evening. We're going. Both of us. Awake.
then other: family.tease_answer

rule f7_sp_house
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.house
does tell.self
cooldown 3d
say {f7_tease=duty f7_chain=tease} The House expects us at the head's table on the festival. Both of us. Smiling. | {f7_tease=duty f7_chain=tease} Your cousin's steward now. We'll have to call and congratulate them. In person. | {f7_tease=duty f7_chain=tease} We're to wear the House's colours at the festival. Don't argue. | {f7_tease=duty f7_chain=tease} The steward wants us both at the counting of the year. Best coats.
then other: family.tease_answer

rule f7_sp_chapel
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.piety=devout other.piety=ordinary here.day=rest
does tell.self
cooldown 3d
say {f7_tease=duty f7_chain=tease} You'll come to chapel with me. Won't you? | {f7_tease=duty f7_chain=tease} The priest asked after you. Kindly. Pointedly. | {f7_tease=duty f7_chain=tease} One hour on Restday, #dear#. The Bright One gives us all the others. | {f7_tease=duty f7_chain=tease} They're blessing the new bell today. Everyone will be there. Everyone.
then other: family.tease_answer

rule f7_sp_short_tired
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.temper=short self.tired=yes
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_tease=snap f7_chain=tease} Don't. Whatever it is, not now. | {f7_tease=snap f7_chain=tease} If one more person asks me for something today. | {f7_tease=snap f7_chain=tease} I'm going to sit here, and nobody is going to speak. | {f7_tease=snap f7_chain=tease} Every wolf in this town wanted something of me today. Every one.
then other: family.tease_answer

rule f7_sp_tavern
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses here.place=tavern
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_tease=ale f7_chain=tease} One more and then home. One. | {f7_tease=ale f7_chain=tease} You've had three. I've been counting even if you haven't. | {f7_tease=ale f7_chain=tease} Slow down. You'll be singing next, and nobody wants that. | {f7_tease=ale f7_chain=tease} That's your last. I'm telling the keeper.
then other: family.tease_answer

rule f7_sp_merry
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.humour=merry
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_tease=flirt f7_chain=tease} Marry me. | {f7_tease=flirt f7_chain=tease} Remind me, did I marry you for your looks or your cooking? | {f7_tease=flirt f7_chain=tease} If you were a pie, I'd eat you. | {f7_tease=flirt f7_chain=tease} Run away with me. Not far. Just to the tavern. | {f7_tease=flirt f7_chain=tease} Dance with me. Here. Nobody's looking. Everybody's looking.
then other: family.tease_answer

rule f7_sp_dry
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.humour=dry
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
say {f7_tease=jibe f7_chain=tease} You were snoring so loud the neighbours paid us a call. | {f7_tease=jibe f7_chain=tease} I've decided to forgive you. For what, I'll think of later. | {f7_tease=jibe f7_chain=tease} I'm told marriage is a partnership. Which part's yours? | {f7_tease=jibe f7_chain=tease} I've been married to you so long I've started agreeing with you. It's alarming.
then other: family.tease_answer

rule f7_sp_from_apart
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses pair.same_from=no
does tell.self
cooldown 3d
say {f7_tease=jibe f7_chain=tease} You said it again. That word from your home. | {f7_tease=jibe f7_chain=tease} Your lot eat that with honey? Truly? | {f7_tease=jibe f7_chain=tease} Sometimes I can't understand a word your family says. | {f7_tease=jibe f7_chain=tease} You still say it the old way, you know. After all these years.
then other: family.tease_answer

rule f7_sp_old_tease
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.age>=40 other.age>=40
does tell.self
cooldown 3d
say {f7_tease=jibe f7_chain=tease} You were a terror when you were young. You still are. | {f7_tease=jibe f7_chain=tease} I found a grey hair. On you, I mean. Mine are silver. | {f7_tease=jibe f7_chain=tease} Twenty years and you still leave the lid off the crock. | {f7_tease=jibe f7_chain=tease} Would you marry me again? Think carefully.
then other: family.tease_answer

# =============================================================================================== Spouses: fond words, news and plans

rule f7_sp_old_years
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.stage=old other.stage=old
does ask.detail
cooldown 2d
say {f7_share=years f7_chain=share} All those years. Where did they go? | {f7_share=years f7_chain=share} Do you remember the day we met? You had mud to the knees. | {f7_share=years f7_chain=share} Do you remember our first winter? One blanket and a leaking roof. | {f7_share=years f7_chain=share} We've buried a lot of friends, you and me. Still here, though.
then other: family.share_answer

rule f7_sp_old_paws
when concept=talk.family pair.band=spouses self.stage=old other.stage=old here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self
cooldown 2d
